{"name":"Distant Thunder","hex":"#7f8688","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"distant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Far off (physically, logically or mentally).","Emotionally unresponsive or unwilling to express genuine feelings."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distant"},{"term":"thunder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The loud rumbling, cracking, or crashing sound caused by expansion of rapidly heated air around a lightning bolt.","A deep, rumbling noise resembling thunder."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce thunder; to sound, rattle, or roar, as a discharge of atmospheric electricity.","To make a noise like thunder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Distant Thunder (1973 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Distant Thunder is a 1973 Indian Bengali film by director Satyajit Ray, based on an eponymous by Bibhutibhushan Bandopadhyay. \nUnlike most of Ray's earlier films, Distant Thunder was filmed in colour. It stars Soumitra Chatterjee, who headlined numerous Ray films, and the Bangladeshi actress Bobita in her only prominent international role. Today the film features in The New York Times Guide to the Best 1,000 Movies Ever Made. It marked the debut of the theatre star Mrityunjay Sil."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/Dvd_ashani_sanket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distant_Thunder_(1973_film)","wikidata":"Q715026"},{"title":"Distant Thunder (1988 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Distant Thunder is a 1988 American drama film directed by Rick Rosenthal and starring John Lithgow and Ralph Macchio."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Distant_Thunder_%281988_American_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distant_Thunder_(1988_film)","wikidata":"Q5282913"},{"title":"Thunder","blocks":[{"text":"Thunder is the sound caused by lightning. Depending upon the distance from and nature of the lightning, it can range from a long, low rumble to a sudden, loud crack. The sudden increase in temperature and hence pressure caused by the lightning produces rapid expansion of the air in the path of a lightning bolt. In turn, this expansion of air creates a sonic shock wave, often referred to as a \"thunderclap\" or \"peal of thunder\". The scientific study of thunder is known as brontology and the irrational fear (phobia) of thunder is called brontophobia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder","wikidata":"Q83301"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"distant":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/En-us-distant.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/38/En-us-distant.ogg/En-us-distant.ogg.mp3"}],"thunder":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/En-us-thunder.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/